# FoxAI Browser — mozconfig (local development entry file)
#
# Two-layer layout mirrored from BrowserWorks/waterfox: this file only
# selects the dev profile, the real flags live in
# fork/build/mozconfig.common. Behaviour comes from fork/user.js +
# fork/policies.json + fork/patches/ — flags here do NOT change product
# behaviour.
#
# Copy this file to the Waterfox checkout as `mozconfig` (see
# fork/BUILD.md step 1 — fork/ goes into the tree as foxai/ first).
#
# License: MPL-2.0 (repo root LICENSE).

# --- dev profile acknowledgement (required by mozconfig.common) ---
fx_dev=1

# --- the shared fragment does the real work ---
. "$topsrcdir/foxai/build/mozconfig.common"

# --- branding: official branding stays OFF (default) ---
# Do NOT pass --enable-official-branding: FoxAI ships its own artwork
# from fork/branding/ instead of Mozilla/Waterfox trademarks.

# --- reproducible builds: SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH is injected by CI ---
# (.github/workflows/release.yml); for local builds set it to the
# release tag date, e.g.:
#   export SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=$(git log -1 --format=%ct)
#
# (Optimise/LTO/PGO/updater/crashreporter/objdir choices all live in
# fork/build/mozconfig.common — do not duplicate them here.)

# --- Windows (MSVC): keep default toolchain via bootstrap ---
# ./mach bootstrap --application=browser  (accepts MSVC + Win SDK install)
#
# --- Linux (Fedora): system toolchain is fine ---
# sudo dnf builddep firefox  # then ./mach build
#
# --- macOS ---
# Xcode CLT + `ac_add_options --target=x86_64-apple-darwin` /
# `--target=aarch64-apple-darwin` per arch (lipo in packaging step).
